From 9a58d7d5f3abca7fc5046291d21684f480ad4032 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add a file-backed V2 header snapshot and undo log

Persist the caller-supplied header as a versioned checksummed header.dat
plus one numbered undo record per commit. The payload is the chain id,
height, 134-byte SerializeHeader encoding, and the existing BlockId.
Reopen returns the same bytes. Undo of the only record leaves no header;
a later undo restores the previous header bytes, including height. A
truncated record fails closed. This is a header file snapshot, not block
acceptance and not ConnectTip.
